open_file_algorithm {
    When the editor opens or changes a `.rq` buffer, `reqlan-lsp` runs this sequence.
    Do not wait for the ideas index. Do not wait for a workspace crawl.
    Detail: [open_file_sequence_diagram].
    Related: [open_file_reference_sequencing], [language_server_rust], [ast_lifecycle],
    [outbound_one_hop], [open_file_hot_path], [token_colour_sequence],
    [missing_reference_colour_sequence], [lazy_features_after_outbound].

    The hot path finishes before the first diagnostics publish.
    1. Parse this buffer once ([ast_lifecycle]).
    2. Colour tokens from that parse ([token_colour_sequence]).
    3. Emit same-file links and same-file missing-idea errors from that parse.
    4. Parse each imported file once, at depth 1, for idea names and lines ([outbound_one_hop]).
       Link an imported name that exists. Underline an imported name that does not
       ([missing_reference_colour_sequence]).
    5. Return. A qualified reference may link to its file from the path token.
       Do not read that file on this path.

    After that publish, a background pass fills the rest ([lazy_features_after_outbound]).
    That pass must not delay steps 1–5.
    The server sends the hot publish before it starts that pass.
    It runs that pass only while no client message waits. A hover or a definition request goes first.
    A change reuses the import roots loaded at open. It does not read the config again.
    The node engine keeps [node_engine_open_path].

    @status done
    @implementation (
        [lsp_session]
        [lsp_analysis]
        [lsp_server]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../../../crates/reqlan-lsp/tests/session.rs:semantic_token_range_matches_the_source_name"]
        ["../../../../crates/reqlan-lsp/tests/parity.rs:same_file_idea_references_produce_document_links"]
        ["../../../../crates/reqlan-lsp/tests/parity.rs:from_import_binds_a_local_reference"]
        ["../../../../crates/reqlan-lsp/tests/parity.rs:reports_an_error_when_an_imported_idea_does_not_exist"]
        ["../../../../packages/language/test/local-symbolic-links.test.ts:same-file idea links without DocumentBuilder / workspace link"]
    )
}

open_file_sequence_diagram {
    [open_file_algorithm]
    Actors: VS Code editor, TextMate grammar, extension host, `reqlan-lsp`, file system.

    ```mermaid
    sequenceDiagram
        autonumber
        participant User
        participant Editor as VS Code editor
        participant TextMate as TextMate grammar
        participant ExtHost as Extension host
        participant Lsp as reqlan-lsp
        participant Fs as File system

        User->>Editor: Open or change .rq file
        Editor->>TextMate: Tokenise buffer
        TextMate-->>Editor: Immediate syntax colour
        Editor->>ExtHost: didOpen / didChange
        ExtHost->>Lsp: textDocument/didOpen or didChange
        Lsp->>Lsp: Parse this buffer once
        Lsp-->>Editor: Semantic tokens, same-file links, same-file errors
        loop each imported file
            Lsp->>Fs: Read imported file
            Lsp->>Lsp: Parse idea names and lines
        end
        Lsp-->>Editor: Import-target links and import errors
        Note over Lsp: Qualified-reference files stay unread
        Note over Lsp: Index snapshot stays unread
    ```
}

ast_lifecycle {
    The open buffer has one model. That model is the Rust parse of this buffer.
    [local_symbolic_analysis] is a file-local extract. The hot path does not run it as a second parse.
    Related: [open_file_algorithm], [open_file_sequence_diagram], [outbound_one_hop],
    [token_colour_sequence], [parse_budget_timeout],
    ["./initialisation-and-sequencing.rq".lsp_file_watch], [language_server_rust].

    Populate. Parse this buffer when the editor opens it.
    Semantic tokens, same-file links, and the import list come from that parse.

    Replace. When this buffer text changes, parse again and replace the model.
    Do not patch the old model. A watched `.rq` change uses the same replace path
    ([document_update_handler]). When the text is unchanged, keep the current model.

    Drop. When the editor closes the buffer, drop the model.
    A closed file keeps no syntax tree ([language_server_rust]).

    Import files. [outbound_one_hop] stores a name list for each imported file.
    That list is not an open-buffer model.
    A change to an imported file does not replace this buffer's model.
    Read the imported file again when its content hash changes.

    Incomplete parse. When the budget fails, store an empty model plus diagnostics
    ([parse_budget_timeout]). Idea names stay empty until a later successful parse.

    The node engine follows [node_engine_open_path].

    @status done
    @implementation (
        [lsp_session]
        [lsp_analysis]
        [lsp_server]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../../../crates/reqlan-lsp/tests/session.rs:open_file_diagnostics_and_close_drops_the_parse"]
        ["../../../../packages/language/test/parse-budget.test.ts:times out a hung parse worker with warning and error"]
    )
}

token_colour_sequence {
    Token colour has two layers. They must not wait for the ideas index.
    TextMate paints first from the buffer text. Semantic tokens paint from the one parse
    ([ast_lifecycle]). A second extract does not paint tokens.
    A missing reference keeps the same token colour. The error underline is a diagnostic
    ([missing_reference_colour_sequence], [reference_rendering]).
    Related: [syntax_highlighting].

    ```mermaid
    sequenceDiagram
        autonumber
        participant Editor as VS Code editor
        participant TextMate as TextMate grammar
        participant Lsp as reqlan-lsp

        Editor->>TextMate: Buffer text
        TextMate-->>Editor: Scopes for ideas, imports, links, comments
        Editor->>Lsp: semanticTokens/full
        Lsp->>Lsp: Walk the one parse
        Lsp-->>Editor: Types, namespaces, strings, variables, keywords, methods
    ```

    @status done
    @implementation (
        ["../../../../packages/language/syntaxes/reqlan.tmLanguage.json"]
        ["../../../../packages/extension/package.json"]
        ["../../../../crates/reqlan-lsp/src/server.rs"]
        [semantic_tokens]
        [lsp_analysis]
        [language_server_main]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../../../packages/language/test/textmate-import-highlight.test.ts"]
        ["../../../../packages/language/test/semantic-tokens-wildcard.test.ts"]
        ["../../../../crates/reqlan-lsp/tests/session.rs:semantic_token_range_matches_the_source_name"]
        ["../../../../crates/reqlan-lsp/tests/session.rs:semantic_tokens_cover_import_keywords_and_file_symbols"]
    )
}

file_crawl_sequence {
    Workspace crawl is the indexer ([index], [index_sequencing]). It is not the open-file path.
    Native sync walks `.rq` files, then allowlisted code files, and writes SQLite.
    Open-file links must not wait for that walk ([open_file_algorithm]).
    The language server watches `.rq` files only (["./initialisation-and-sequencing.rq".lsp_file_watch]).
    Related: [extension_startup_sequence], [background_startup].

    ```mermaid
    sequenceDiagram
        autonumber
        participant ExtHost as Extension host
        participant Native as Native sync
        participant Fs as File system
        participant Sqlite as SQLite index
        participant Lsp as reqlan-lsp
        participant Editor as VS Code editor

        ExtHost->>Native: Soft syncWorkspace (mtime skip)
        Native->>Fs: Walk .rq files then code files
        Native->>Sqlite: Upsert ideas and edges
        Note over Lsp,Editor: Open-file links do not wait for this walk
        Sqlite-->>ExtHost: Index ready
        ExtHost->>Lsp: Push inbound snapshot for visible editors
        Lsp-->>Editor: Backlinks when the snapshot arrives
    ```

    @status done
    @implementation (
        ["../../../../packages/analytical/src/index-store/workspace-index.ts"]
        ["../../../../crates/reqlan-index/src/sync.rs"]
        [inbound_sync]
        [lsp_server]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../../../packages/analytical/test/workspace-index.test.ts"]
    )
}

outbound_one_hop {
    The hot path parses imported files only.
    For each import in the open buffer, parse that file once, then stop.
    Read idea names, idea lines, and import aliases. Do not parse files that the import references.
    Do not read SQLite.
    Prefer the open buffer text when that import is already open and dirty.
    Cache each parse by path plus file stamp (modified time and size) ([lsp_session]).
    A current stamp is one `stat`. Read and parse the file only when the stamp changed.
    Cache the open buffer by URI plus text fingerprint ([open_file_hot_path]).
    [local_symbolic_analysis] stays file-local. This hop is outside that extract.
    An extensionless import path prefers `.rq`, then the path as written
    ([implicit_file_extension]).
    A qualified reference that is not an import waits for [lazy_features_after_outbound].
    Related: [open_file_algorithm], [non_web_reference_navigation].

    @status done
    @implementation (
        [lsp_session]
        [lsp_analysis]
        [native_parse]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../../../crates/reqlan-lsp/tests/parity.rs:from_import_tokens_link_independently"]
        ["../../../../crates/reqlan-lsp/tests/parity.rs:reports_an_error_when_an_import_path_file_does_not_exist"]
        ["../../../../crates/reqlan-lsp/tests/parity.rs:extensionless_path_confirms_the_neighbor_idea"]
        ["../../../../packages/language/test/outbound-hop.test.ts:reuses a cached neighbor parse for the same content"]
        ["../../../../packages/language/test/outbound-hop.test.ts:does not parse a neighbor of the neighbor"]
    )
}

open_file_hot_path {
    Open-file work stays on the one parse of this buffer plus one parse per imported file.
    Reuse that model for document links, go-to-definition, hover, and diagnostics until the text
    or the import-root mapping changes.
    Keep that model, and the import name lists, only for open editors ([native_cache_retention]).
    Look up an open import by URI. Do not match on file basename.
    Do not read SQLite. Do not call `list_all_ideas`.
    At parse time, publish lex and parse diagnostics with same-file and import errors.
    The editor must not wait for a workspace link phase to see a broken parse.
    Handlers on this path read the open model. They do not build a workspace link graph.
    Related: [open_file_algorithm], [outbound_one_hop], [ast_lifecycle],
    [comment_backlink_sequence].

    @status in-progress
    @todo Unqualified comment lookup can still fall back to the name catalog when no open buffer matches.
    @implementation (
        [lsp_session]
        [lsp_analysis]
        [lsp_server]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../../../packages/language/test/open-file-hot-path.test.ts:reuses the host native extract for links and diagnostics"]
        ["../../../../packages/language/test/open-file-hot-path.test.ts:reparses the host native extract when this buffer text changes"]
        ["../../../../packages/language/test/open-file-hot-path.test.ts:does not treat a same-name file as the loaded neighbor"]
        ["../../../../crates/reqlan-lsp/tests/parity.rs:same_file_idea_references_produce_document_links"]
    )
}

missing_reference_colour_sequence {
    Paint links and errors in two steps.
    The hot path paints same-file names and import targets ([outbound_one_hop]).
    The background pass paints qualified-reference idea lines ([lazy_features_after_outbound]).
    Related: [unresolved_reference_diagnostics], [reference_rendering],
    [file_reference_errors], [import_does_not_exist_error].

    Hot path:
    - URL references: document link, no error.
    - Wildcard references: document link, no error underline for zero matches.
    - Import path missing: error underline, no document link.
    - Imported idea present: document link to that idea line.
    - Imported idea missing: error underline, no document link.
    - Same-file idea missing: error underline, no document link.
    - Qualified reference: document link to the file from the path token.
      Do not underline a missing idea yet.

    Background pass:
    - Qualified idea present: document link to that idea line.
    - Qualified idea missing: error underline, and remove the document link.
    - Drop a false missing-idea error only for the range that this pass confirms.
      Keep a different missing name on the same line.

    @status done
    @implementation (
        [lsp_analysis]
        [lsp_session]
        [outbound_presentation]
        [document_links]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../../../crates/reqlan-lsp/tests/parity.rs:missing_file_references_do_not_produce_document_links"]
        ["../../../../packages/language/test/outbound-hop.test.ts:keeps URL and wildcard document links"]
        ["../../../../packages/language/test/outbound-hop.test.ts:keeps a missing idea error on the same line as a confirmed neighbor idea"]
        ["../../../../packages/language/test/local-symbolic-links.test.ts:unresolved same-file ideas get no document link"]
    )
}

comment_backlink_sequence {
    `rq:[idea]` and `rq:["path".idea]` in code comments use one resolution for the link and the underline.
    A qualified path reads that `.rq` file, parses idea names, then links or errors.
    That read belongs to the comment file. Opening a different `.rq` buffer must not re-resolve every comment buffer.
    An unqualified name searches open `.rq` buffers first.
    The index snapshot may add a match later ([lazy_features_after_outbound]).
    Do not call `list_all_ideas` for that search.
    Do not create an idea link when the idea is not confirmed.
    Keep the path link when that same resolution found the file ([comment_reference_resolution_error_state]).
    Related: [comment_reference_resolution_error_state].

    @status in-progress
    @todo A change to a .rq file still republishes every comment buffer in the background pass, and unqualified lookup can call list_all_ideas.
    @implementation (
        [lsp_session]
        [comment_diagnostics]
        [comment_links_host]
        ["../../../../packages/language/src/reqlan-comment-resolver.ts"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../../../crates/reqlan-lsp/tests/session.rs:comment_links_share_one_resolution"]
        ["../../../../packages/language/test/comment-reference-resolution.test.ts:reports a missing comment reference idea in a loaded file"]
        ["../../../../packages/language/test/comment-reference-resolution.test.ts:shares one presentation so a matching idea clears the underline and adds a link"]
    )
}

lazy_features_after_outbound {
    After the hot path is on screen, show the rest when its data is ready.
    This pass must not delay [open_file_algorithm] steps 1–5.
    Related: [language_server], [unify_inbound_indexes], [background_startup],
    [inlay_hints], [codelens].

    Work:
    - Confirm each qualified reference. Read that target file once, at depth 1.
      Then paint the idea line or the missing-idea error ([missing_reference_colour_sequence]).
    - Inbound backlinks: inlay hints and the file-top CodeLens, from the host snapshot
      ([unify_inbound_indexes]).
    - Attribute and name catalogs for completion and quick fixes.
    - Unqualified comment matches from that snapshot ([comment_backlink_sequence]).

    Until the first ready snapshot arrives, inlay hints and the file CodeLens stay empty.
    Those handlers do not open SQLite and do not call `list_all_ideas`.
    Later updates are incremental ready-state events
    (["../../../indexer/cache-reuse.rq".inbound_snapshot_events]); last-good stays until replaced.
    When a ready snapshot arrives, refresh the visible editors.

    ```mermaid
    sequenceDiagram
        autonumber
        participant Lsp as reqlan-lsp
        participant Fs as File system
        participant ExtHost as Extension host
        participant Editor as VS Code editor

        Note over Lsp,Editor: Hot path already published
        Lsp->>Fs: Read each qualified-reference file
        Lsp-->>Editor: Idea-line links or missing-idea errors
        ExtHost->>Lsp: Inbound snapshot
        Lsp-->>Editor: Inlay hints, file CodeLens, catalogs
    ```

    @status done
    @implementation (
        [lsp_session]
        [lsp_server]
        [inbound_sync]
        ["../../../../packages/extension/src/extension/main.ts"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../../../packages/language/test/inbound-referencer-index-perf.test.ts:inlay referencers come from the pushed snapshot, not findAllReferences"]
        ["../../../../crates/reqlan-lsp/tests/session.rs:index_completion_inlay_and_custom_requests"]
        ["../../../../crates/reqlan-lsp/tests/session.rs:neighbor_confirm_suppresses_missing_idea"]
        ["../../../../crates/reqlan-lsp/tests/parity.rs:formats_inbound_referencers_as_an_inlayed_attribute"]
    )
}

native_cache_retention {
    The language server keeps the open-buffer model for each open editor.
    It keeps a depth-1 name list for each imported file, and for each qualified-reference file
    the background pass has confirmed, while an open editor still needs that list.
    A closed editor drops its model. It also drops name lists that no open editor still needs.
    A file-watcher delete drops that URI from both caches.
    A check of a closed file may parse it once. That result is not stored.
    Related: [open_file_hot_path], [outbound_one_hop], [ast_lifecycle].

    @status done
    @implementation (
        [lsp_session]
        [editor_retention]
        [neighbor_parse]
        [document_update_handler]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../../../crates/reqlan-lsp/tests/session.rs:open_file_diagnostics_and_close_drops_the_parse"]
        ["../../../../packages/language/test/lsp-memory.test.ts:drops a neighbor list when the last open editor closes"]
        ["../../../../packages/language/test/lsp-memory.test.ts:drops a neighbor list when the file watcher reports a delete"]
        ["../../../../packages/language/test/outbound-hop.test.ts:reuses a cached neighbor parse for the same content"]
    )
}

node_engine_open_path {
    This idea applies when `reqlan.languageServer.engine` is `node`.
    The default engine is [language_server_rust].
    The node server populates a Langium AST for the open buffer at `DocumentState.Parsed`.
    Later builder phases attach scopes, links, and diagnostics. They must not replace that AST.
    Parsed-time handlers must not read Langium `.ref`.
    Use `$refText`, the symbolic extract, or `peekResolvedRef` until `ComputedScopes`.
    The linker must not resolve a cross-reference while that document is below `ComputedScopes`.
    Do not log the Langium warning. Do not store a failed link.
    Scope lookup, code lens, completion, and idea summaries use `readResolvedRef` or `peekResolvedRef` until that phase.
    When another `.rq` file changes, relink this document when the index says it is affected,
    when comment references name that file, or when this document's outbound targets include the changed URI.
    Do not relink every document that still has a linker error.
    Workspace load parses at most 8 files at a time ([workspace_parse_concurrency]).
    `fileIdeasCache` and `importPathCache` drop a URI when that document is removed ([scope_cache_release]).
    Related: [open_file_algorithm], [ast_lifecycle].

    @status done
    @implementation (
        [document_factory]
        [document_builder]
        [async_parser]
        [parse_budget]
        [workspace_manager]
        [scope_provider]
        [local_symbolic_links]
        [neighbor_parse]
        [outbound_presentation]
        [document_links]
        [language_server_main]
        ["../../../../packages/language/src/reqlan-linker.ts"]
        ["../../../../packages/language/src/reqlan-reference-peek.ts"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../../../packages/language/test/ast-lifecycle.test.ts:populates the Langium AST at Parsed without DocumentBuilder"]
        ["../../../../packages/language/test/ast-lifecycle.test.ts:linking and validation do not replace the AST"]
        ["../../../../packages/language/test/ast-lifecycle.test.ts:neighbor hop does not populate a Langium AST"]
        ["../../../../packages/language/test/parsed-reference-sequencing.test.ts:definition hover highlight and links do not resolve refs before ComputedScopes"]
        ["../../../../packages/language/test/parsed-reference-sequencing.test.ts:reading every ref before ComputedScopes does not warn and linking still works"]
        ["../../../../packages/language/test/open-file-hot-path.test.ts:does not relink an unrelated file that still has linker errors"]
        ["../../../../packages/language/test/open-file-hot-path.test.ts:relinks a host when its neighbor file changes"]
    )
}

scope_cache_release {
    This idea applies when the engine is `node` ([node_engine_open_path]).
    `fileIdeasCache` and `importPathCache` drop a URI when that Langium document is removed.
    A version change still replaces the entry for a document that stays.
    The rust server drops the open model in [native_cache_retention].
    Related: [open_file_hot_path], [native_cache_retention].

    @status done
    @implementation (
        [scope_provider]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../../../packages/language/test/lsp-memory.test.ts:drops scope cache entries when a document is removed"]
    )
}

workspace_parse_concurrency {
    This idea applies when the engine is `node` ([node_engine_open_path]).
    Workspace load parses `.rq` files with a fixed limit of 8 in flight.
    One file that fails to parse does not cancel the other files.
    The steady-state set is still every workspace `.rq` file.
    The rust server does not parse the workspace. A closed file keeps no syntax tree
    ([language_server_rust]).
    Related: [ast_lifecycle], [workspace_manager].

    @status done
    @implementation (
        [workspace_manager]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../../../packages/language/test/lsp-memory.test.ts:runs at most the concurrency limit"]
        ["../../../../packages/language/test/lsp-memory.test.ts:loads every workspace file with at most 8 parses in flight"]
    )
}
